59
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:18,860
Okay, smile.

60
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,800
In three, two, one!

61
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:36,940
Mr. Gato?

62
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:42,440
Where'd you go?

63
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,977
I don't know how, but we
must have gotten separated.

64
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,320
I have to find him.

65
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:54,040
There you are.

66
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:57,060
What's wrong?

67
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,700
Oh, my God.

68
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,310
I don't know.

69
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:30,750
Shiori.

70
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,620
Dad, but you're dead.

71
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:46,100
You're at a crossroads between life and
death as a sacrifice to Lord Cladney.

72
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:51,904
Who'd have thought I'd end up getting a
chance to drink with my precious daughter?

73
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,860
Please, father. You told me.

74
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,727
Why did you pick me to
take over the company?

75
